  adversely  tala the u.n high commissioner for human  rights has called for calm is that  enough is the international community in  ethiopia's neighbours doing enough to  call for khan  well i think that effort is okay but uh  the fact is i couldn't agree more that  there has to be far greater effort  and far greater focus actually what  happens is that the major powers are  least interested in these areas and they  think that these humans are not  important and this is one of the saddest  commentary that you can  see  what's happening in the sense that and  there is not a realization at the global  level  even at the african level and that what  is happening  in this part of the world so i think and  it's a sad reflection of the overall  quality of leadership and i think the un  also has to be far more active  although i think  the u.n rights chief did  is taking a lot of interest but that is  not enough uh i think the united nations  security council the u.n  organizations the african countries i  think they all should really focus on  that and should america and also the  major powers china and russia also  should take some interest if they are  responsible major powers  so just how critical is this meeting to  be held by the east african block later  this month what needs to be what is to  happen in that meeting  yeah well i think  they might come out with some sort of a  conciliatory approach but whether will  that be accepted by the parties  concerned that is a big question  well we appreciate your insights talat  massoud a retired lieutenant general and  military analyst thank you for your time  thank you
 

